    "description": "Laffs PDW XL Sights: Laffs Dynamics\n\nTaller variant of the original 3FTech/Laffs PDW Sights. \n\nHave gotten numerous requests for a taller version over last couple years. \n\nRaised it up 8mm. Still uses previous version's swappable rear sight inserts and same set screw for the front sight post.\n\n\nThree rear drift sights are available:\n\n *4mm U Notch\n *5mm U Notch\n *5.5mm Aperture\n\n\n\nNote: For those people that wanted it \"AR\" height... no :D \n\nI aint raising them up 30mm+. They'd be bulky as fuck and they're meant for guns like the Scorpion Evo 3, PS90, GHM9, and Stribog SP9. These sights \nare not precise enough for carbine use in my opinion, and I don't wanna hear people complain about accuracy if I made such a variant. They're fine for \nPDW/SMG/PCC usage. \n\n\n\nOriginal Laffs PDW Sights files can be found on Odysee: \n\nLink: https://odysee.com/@FFFTech:3/3FTech-PDW-Sights:5\n\n\n\nPrinter Used: Ender 3 V2\n\nFilament Used: PLA+\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 220C \nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .20mm \nStandard Layer Height: .12mm\nWall Thickness: .40mm\nWall Perimeters: 6+\nInfill: 50%+\nSupport Material Percentage: 20%\n\nPrint the front and rear sight mounts on their front faces, and the rear sight drift on it's rear, flattest face.\n\n\n\nHardware Needed: \n\n2x M5x30 Hex Socketed Machine Screw/Bolt\n\n2x M5 Hex Nut (Be sure both bolt & nut are the same thread pitch.)\n\n1x M3x10 Set Screw",
